## What about Linux when you use Windows?

You can begin on your existing Windows installation.

However, I recommend supporting two build targets eventually:

- Windows: GCC/MinGW, Command Prompt, GDB and Winsock.
- Linux: GCC or Clang, GDB, POSIX threads and POSIX sockets.

This is an important design consideration. C is portable, but operating-system interfaces are not automatically interchangeable.

We should separate portable database logic from OS-specific networking and threading code.

